{"kind":"report","text":"READY-FOR-REVIEW at exact clean head 7df7003e12872bf3f07a9d86874f296f98dacb06 on request/ambient-live-attention-v2, pushed to origin. Candidates: d4f57522 at internal/nexus, 1b0834e4 at internal/service, 1ade4ab4 at cmd/gitseq-mcp, c05491d3 at docs. All four are non-stale.\n\nBOTH FINDINGS CLOSED, AND BOTH WERE REAL.\n\nThe cross-repository defect was worse than I had assessed. I raised attachedRoom to you myself as the boundary I was least sure of, but I framed it as a multi-repo session getting no attention. You saw that it could get another repository's attention: a call naming one workroom with arguments.repo could be answered with a different workroom's addressed inbox and leased focus. That is a disclosure across a boundary the caller drew deliberately, not a gap.\n\nThe cause was structural rather than local. The adjunct chose its room after the call instead of using the room the call acted in. call now returns that exact room on every path including errors, and the adjunct reads it and nothing else. I deleted attachedRoom rather than leaving it unused, because an after-the-fact room chooser sitting in the file is a trap for whoever next needs a room.\n\nThe pattern defect is closed the same way you described. eventIDPattern now requires a non-identifier byte on each side, so a canonical-looking identifier cannot be cut out of the middle of a longer token, and the scan resumes from the end of each captured identifier so two separated by a single delimiter both survive.\n\nMUTATION-VERIFIED, INCLUDING ONE I HAD TO REDO. Returning the adapter default instead of the acted room fails the two-repository test, and the failure names both repository paths. Removing the boundaries fails the boundary test on the leading-byte case. My first attempt at the room mutation did not compile, which proves nothing, so I rewrote it as one that does before trusting the result.\n\nGATES AT THIS EXACT HEAD. git diff --check clean, go vet clean, make test with no failures, go test -race on internal/nexus, internal/service and cmd/gitseq-mcp, and an uncached internal/docset run. The head commit carries Rests-On with this request's full canonical ID.\n\nSUCCESSION. Replacements were published before anything was retired. Both dead candidate sets are now retired — the four at ea570287 and the four at d3506e02 — all eight effective, verified from projection.acts. Each path now carries exactly the shipped predecessor and this candidate, both non-stale.\n\nYou have now found three things I missed across three reviews: provenance, the missing commit trailer, and the room selection. Two of those were invisible in the artifacts I published, and the third I had looked at and misjudged. I would rather you kept finding them than agreed with me.","body":{"branch":"request/ambient-live-attention-v2","head":"7df7003e12872bf3f07a9d86874f296f98dacb06","status":"ready-for-review"}}